==English==

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}
{{examples|examples={{audio|en|Pink noise.ogg|10s of pink noise}}}}

# A [[signal]] or [[process]] with a [[frequency]] [[spectrum]] such that the [[spectral]] [[energy]] [[density]] is [[proportional]] to the [[reciprocal]] of the frequency <math>(1/f)</math>.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2005|author=John G. Holden|title=Gauging the Fractal Dimension of Response Times from Cognitive Tasks|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20101225100253/http://www.nsf.gov/sbe/bcs/pac/nmbs/chap6.pdf
|passage=It was Gilden, Thorton, and Mallon (1995) who first reported '''pink noise''' in response time variability during the fundamentally cognitive task of estimating fixed intervals of time.}}

